Legitimate reads beside the new rules (should pass):
  PASS: a property literally named in a string after a comment
  PASS: a backtick-quoted label holding a keyword is an identifier, not a clause
  PASS: a function that is not on the blocked prefix list
  PASS: an unterminated string literal is refused, never guessed at

Regular-expression operator (should fail; the literal case should pass):
  PASS: R1 refused: MATCH (n) WHERE n.name =~ '(a+)+$' RETURN n
  PASS: R2 refused: MATCH (n) WHERE n.name=~'.*RefId' RETURN count(n)
  PASS: R3 refused: MATCH (n) WITH n, '(?i).*student.*' AS p WHERE n.description =~ p RETURN n.name
  PASS: R4 refused: MATCH (n) RETURN [x IN n.aliases WHERE x =~ "(\w+\s?)*"] AS hits
  PASS: =~ inside a string literal is text, not the operator

